{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id1438845983"}, "name":{"label":"stevestevsteve"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-15T07:23:53-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2026.272"}, "id":{"label":"14669724725"}, "title":{"label":"Unbelievably frustrating"}, "content":{"label":"I’m genuinely fed up with ChatGPT’s image editing.\n\nA simple request to add a small cross necklace to an existing image, without changing anything else, has turned into an exhausting exercise in frustration.\n\nAround 45 out of 50 attempts result in some ridiculous warning about scam activity, despite the request having absolutely nothing to do with scams, fraud, or anything remotely suspicious.\n\nOn the rare occasions the request actually gets through, the model still manages to get it wrong. It changes parts of the image that I specifically instructed it to leave untouched.\n\nThe instructions couldn’t be clearer: Do not alter anything. Just add the necklace.\n\nYet somehow, this basic task becomes a battle against false safety warnings, inconsistent results, and a model that seemingly cannot follow straightforward instructions.\n\nWhat’s particularly infuriating is the amount of time wasted repeating the same request over and over, trying to get something that should have worked the first time.\n\nThis isn’t a complicated editing job. It’s adding one small accessory to a picture.\n\nIf a paid AI service cannot reliably distinguish a harmless image edit from scam activity, and then cannot follow basic instructions when it finally allows the edit, there is a serious problem with both its moderation system and its image-editing capabilities.\n\nI’m not asking for miracles. I’m asking for the service to do what it’s told without falsely flagging innocent requests or unnecessarily altering the original image.\n\nAt this point, the experience feels less like using a helpful AI tool and more like fighting against the software just to accomplish the simplest task.\n\nOne star. Not because the technology lacks potential, but because the actual user experience is unbelievably frustrating.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=6448311069&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
